---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Add objects of one kind to a board; the kind word is the default kind of every --items item.
Without --at each goes to a free corner, in --frame if given, else in the frame a linked object sits in. It prints one line per object with @N and its link.
An image or a file is uploaded first; a link card takes its title from the page. With --items, #N names an earlier item as an arrow end, and one write holds all of them.

USAGE
  holst object add task <board> [<text>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name
  text    The text; lines become paragraphs; the title of a frame or task; the code of a code block; the name of an icon, e.g. rocket-launch

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws       Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --frame frame        Put it inside this frame: id, link, title or part of a title; --at counts from its corner
      --at x,y             The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
  -c, --color color        The fill, or an arrow's line color: a palette token, e.g. yellow4; a task's: gray, green, yellow, orange, red, violet, blue, sky, lime or pink; a drawing's line: a palette token; #1E1E1E (#FBF040 highlighter) by default; the kind's own color by default; an icon takes gray12, gray8, red9, orange9, yellow9, lime9, green9, mint9, blue9, indigo9, violet9 or pink9
      --description text   A task's description; the text is its title
      --status status      A task's status: backlog, to-do, in-progress, done, canceled, or the title of a status of the board; none by default
      --start day          The day a task starts, YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2026-11-02; on or before --due
      --due day            The day a task is due, YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2026-11-06
      --column text        A kanban's column, repeat for each, in order; To do, In progress and Done by default; a task's: the title of its column in --kanban, the first by default
      --swimlane text      A kanban's swimlane, repeat for each, in order; one, Untitled, by default; a task's: the title of its swimlane in --kanban, the first by default
      --kanban object      The kanban a task goes into, as a card in its cell: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id; --column and --swimlane pick the cell; left out with --at and --frame
      --items file         Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
  -n, --dry-run            Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o add task "Roadmap" "Ship" --status in-progress --due 2026-11-06

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
